"Levels are \\(20\\log_{10}(a_n/a_{\\rm ref})\\) with the strongest partial as the {#} dB reference (in the spectrum, the top of a bar); the RMS is \\(\\sqrt{\\tfrac12\\sum_n a_n^2}\\) in bar units; the repetition period comes from the greatest common factor of the harmonic numbers present, and a tone with a detuned or stretched partial never repeats exactly. Equal temperament: \\(f = 440\\ \\text{Hz}\\times 2^{k/12},\\) k semitones from A4.",
"Square wave, Sawtooth wave and Triangle wave are the exact Fourier series cut off at {#} harmonics, which causes the ripples near the jumps: \\(a_n = 1/n\\) for every harmonic (sawtooth), \\(a_n = 1/n\\) for odd n (square) and \\(a_n = 1/n^2\\) for odd n with harmonics {#}, {#}, {#} and {#} inverted (triangle). The Like a clarinet and Like a flute presets and the instrument slider are illustrative spectra chosen to show one feature, not measurements of real instruments.",
"Inharmonic partials: a detuned harmonic is shifted by Δf, so the shape drifts through a full cycle every \\(1/\\lvert \\Delta f\\rvert\\); stiffness stretches every partial as \\(f_n = n f_1\\sqrt{\\frac{1 + Bn^2}{1 + B}},\\) scaled so partial {#} stays at \\(f_1\\). The ladder shows ideal string and pipe modes with no end correction, slowed so f₁ is drawn at {#} Hz.",
"The readings are simulated: the tone is synthesized, not recorded.",
